10017	{"artifactId":"LLD-8315a11f29fd2812-s3","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-8315a11f29fd2812-s3-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-20T19:56:18.465Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design addresses all four upstream S003 acceptance criteria.","evidence":"DEF §6.3 and HLD §5.3 require obligation adjudication, cross-chunk relationship checks, duplicate detection and the installed-daemon smoke. The design assigns these to obligation gather, relationCall, compare/pair and the smoke respectively. The existing adapters implement the first three mechanisms; the relationship-completeness dependency gap is reported under change-sites. [files: docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/DEF.md, docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/HLD.md, src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-gather.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-duplicates.ts]","action":"Retain this scope and resolve the relationship dependency gap.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today's quality review reasons over structured symbol summaries rather than function bodies.","evidence":"buildQualityPrompt explicitly says 'Reason only over the structured symbol summaries provided — you are not given raw file contents' and serializes grounding.symbols. ChangedSymbolSummary carries signatures and caller/callee names. codeReviewMaterial serializes those same rows into atoms. [files: src/workflow/code-review/dimensions/quality.ts, src/workflow/code-review/types.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-material.ts]","action":"Preserve the stated limitation; do not treat signature-only evidence as proof of body-level behavior.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The verdict fold remains HIGH→block, MED→warn, otherwise pass, with an optional pass-to-warn floor.","evidence":"runCodeReview collects dimension results serially and folds their findings. foldVerdict computes 'counts.high > 0 ? block : counts.med > 0 ? warn : pass'; capAtWarn promotes only pass. outOfScope findings are excluded from foldCounts. [files: src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts]","action":"Keep the existing fold unchanged.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shared pipeline already supplies the finish-before-merge contract, refusal hooks and completion hook this Story consumes.","evidence":"GatherPlan exposes obligationCall with context, relationCall with maxChars, validate and merge. AdapterStage exposes carries-related redivision through redivide. finishJob invokes adapter.finish before gather.merge([finished, ...parts]). RunReviewJobOpts exposes onDone, invoked with the finished job. runDimensionJob does not yet install the proposed plan logging, consistent with the design identifying it as remaining work. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/types.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/code-review.ts]","action":"Reuse these contracts and add the planned logging at runDimensionJob.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Consuming s2's crossRelations is sufficient to check every directed caller–callee relationship cut between chunks.","evidence":"codeReviewMaterial deduplicates all relations using 'const [a, b] = from < to ? [from, to] : [to, from]' and 'JSON.stringify([kind, a, b])', including calls. A read-only execution with A calling B and B calling A produced only [{\"from\":\"a\",\"to\":\"b\",\"kind\":\"calls\"}]. planChunks merely filters material.relations into crossRelations; startGather forwards each retained direction, and relationCall judges the first atom as caller. Consequently, the reverse call's argument/return/error contract gets no dedicated relationship check. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-material.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/prepare.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-gather.ts]","action":"Record an explicit dependency correction in s2: preserve ordered endpoints for calls while retaining unordered deduplication for symmetric relations. Add a mutual-call fixture split across chunks and require both directed checks.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Divided finish returns unfiltered chunk findings and merge applies the dimension result filters once.","evidence":"modelDimensionAdapter.finish returns chunkFindings for divided reviews. codeReviewGather.merge calls finalize(mergeFindings(parts)); finalize invokes spec.toResult and separately retains out-of-set findings for the controller. finishJob supplies obligation and relation parts after finish. Existing gather tests assert deduplication, FR filtering, controller outOfScope preservation and one coverage lowering. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/code-review.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/adapters/code-review-gather.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/code-review-gather.test.ts]","action":"Preserve this ordering when completing integration.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Optional pipelineCalls can be added without rewriting existing code-review records or removing parts.","evidence":"DimensionResult retains optional parts and defines optional pipelineCalls. pipelineCallsOf returns undefined for a single-chunk plan; finishJob adds the field only when defined. The runner persists dimension results directly, and enforceCodeReviewGate reads verdict/counts without requiring either diagnostics field. [files: src/workflow/code-review/types.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts, src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts]","action":"Keep both fields optional and leave older records untouched.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"S003 owns code-review gather and the acceptance smoke, while generic pipeline machinery, material construction and controller integration belong to adjacent Stories.","evidence":"HLD §5 assigns the generic pipeline and sc1–sc6 to s1, code-review material to s2, gather and smoke to s3, design review to s4 and controller frames to s5. The design follows that allocation and consumes existing adapter hooks rather than introducing a replacement protocol. [files: docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/HLD.md, src/workflow/review-pipeline/types.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/code-review.ts]","action":"Route the directed-call prerequisite correction through s2's ownership rather than silently expanding S003.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An invalid or failed gather call is retried once, then fails the review without writing a new partial review record.","evidence":"applyFailure assigns gather roles onCallFailure:'fail-review', reissues while attempt is below MAX_CALL_ATTEMPTS, and otherwise throws ReviewCallFailedError. Size refusals take separate redivision branches. runReviewJob propagates terminal failures; runCodeReview catches them before its artifact-writing phase and returns {ok:false,error}. This does not delete a record from an earlier successful run. [files: src/workflow/review-pipeline/job.ts, src/workflow/review-pipeline/driver.ts, src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts]","action":"Retain the planned end-to-end assertion that a terminal gather failure causes no new record write.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every upstream acceptance criterion has a designated test in the design.","evidence":"DEF S003 ac1–ac4 map to divided/single equivalence, relationship mismatch, duplicate reporting and installed-daemon smoke. PLAN t8 and t9 carry the integration and smoke work. Existing code-review-gather tests exercise obligations, relationship dispatch, pair-result merging, validation and normalization. The dedicated divided integration and live smoke suites are still planned, matching the design's remaining-work statement; their outcomes were not verified. [files: docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/DEF.md, docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/S003/PLAN.md, docs/epics/chunked-review-pipeline-every-review-E202610198315a11f/S003/BUILD.md, src/workflow/review-pipeline/__tests__/code-review-gather.test.ts]","action":"Complete t8/t9 and add the mutual-call regression identified above before claiming acceptance.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":1,"med":0,"low":9,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-20T19:56:18.465Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6-astra","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
